From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:49:22 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(delegate): a subagent that does not settle no longer
 holds the restart's hand-over of the others

With gateway.restart_turn_handoff_per_turn and delegation.restart_handoff the old gateway carries the background subagents and their helpers to their step boundaries, then hands them and the background processes to the next gateway, which adopts the subagents once the processes are handed (0138). The subagent carry waited until every unit had settled, for up to the whole boundary window (the carry ceiling less 60 s, 1020 s at 1080). In a live rollout a helper finished its foreground command inside the carry, its subagent stopped a second later, and the old gateway still sent no process handoff until the ceiling: every handed-off subagent of the instance was resumed about 18 minutes late. Two waits could hold it so: a unit whose children all stopped but whose runner did not return (a teardown that hangs), and a stop waiting for a carried child (or a subagent's helper) that left its turn without recording its boundary.

Both are bounded now. A carried child is waited for only while it is in its turn or recording its boundary; one that left its turn without reaching its boundary is given 5 s and then stopped as at the end of the window. A unit whose handoff stopped all its children and that has not settled 10 s later (UNIT_SETTLE_SECONDS) is recorded as handed off on its own, with the state its handoff kept and the children that had finished, and the restart goes on: the processes are handed over and the next gateway adopts every unit at once. The stuck runner's own finalize later updates the record while this gateway still owns it and changes nothing once the next gateway adopted it. A child still in a carried step (a foreground command, a model call) is waited for as before.
